)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Commands on the List Panels              !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}
}  On ST, DA, I, O, H, PR, INIT and the Job Data Set panel:
}
{  Enter            }With an empty command line: the list read again.
{  UP, DOWN         }Scroll by the SCROLL amount (PF7, PF8).
{  TOP, BOTTOM      }To the first or the last row.
{  FIND string      }The next row whose line holds the string goes to the
}                   top; PF5 (RFIND) finds the next one. NEXT, PREV,
}                   FIRST, LAST and ALL as on the log (topic 12 of the
}                   contents).
{  LOCATE n, L n    }Row n goes to the top.
{  RIGHT, LEFT      }Where a row is wider than the screen: PF11, PF10.
{  ?                }ST, I: the further fields; DA: the other order.
{  END              }Back to the menu; from the Job Data Set panel, back
}                   to the list.
}
}  On a list, FIND looks at the rows as the screen shows them; WORD,
}  PREFIX, SUFFIX and columns are taken but make no difference there.
}
}  The panel commands ST, DA, I, O, H, PR, INIT and LOG go to that panel.
}
}  Enter: commands on every panel   PF10: back   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFKALL
  &ZUP = ISFHTOC
)END
